PhaseShift: L2 tagged next-N-sector stream prefetcher in SimX (per L2 bank).
Applied ONLY to the sixth tree vortex-trees/pspf (scripts/mk_vortex_tree.sh --patchset ps --name pspf, then `git apply --index` of this file); never part of any patchset.
Off unless the environment variable PS_PF_DEPTH is non-zero (and then only in the L2, marked by Cluster): with PS_PF_DEPTH unset the bank is bit-identical to the ps patchset (checked: cycles equal the stored psx rows).
Knobs (environment, read once): PS_PF_DEPTH (sectors per miss trigger = window depth), PS_PF_STEP (sectors per tagged-hit trigger, default 1), PS_PF_QSIZE (candidate queue entries, default 8),
PS_PF_RESERVE (MSHR entries kept for demand misses, default 4), PS_PF_TRIG (bit 0 = trigger on demand read miss, bit 1 = on first hit of a prefetched sector, default 3).
Counters (PSPF line per bank at exit): trig_miss trig_hit queued q_drop redundant issued filled useful late unused_evict unused_end poll_evict[class] poll_miss[class].
Hardware state: 1 tag bit per L2 sector (4096 b at 256 KiB / 64 B sectors), pf + late bit per MSHR entry, a QSIZE-entry candidate queue.
Design and policy are documented in the block comment of CacheBank (cache.cpp, "patch l2-stream-prefetch").

